*> Implementation test of proto/src/chunk-palette.cob: PB-PUT-PALETTE-CONTAINER and
*> PB-GET-PALETTE-CONTAINER on PB-PALETTE-CONTAINER (docs/protocol/06-chunk-format.md §5 and §6),
*> for block states (4096 cells) and biomes (64 cells): single value, indirect at every width the
*> rules of §5.3 allow, direct at the global width, the long packing of §6 and every malformed form.
*> Expected bytes come from the document's rules, computed independently of the codec.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CHUNK-PALETTE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==DC-==.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OFFSET              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KIND                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BITS                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENTRIES             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PALETTE-COUNT       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BASE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STEP                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MODULUS             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MULTIPLIER          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-GLOBAL              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PREFIX              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LONG                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-BYTE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LONGS               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SAME                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TAIL                PIC X(16).
 01 WS-LABEL               PIC X(120).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     PERFORM SINGLE-CASES
     PERFORM BLOCK-INDIRECT-CASES
     PERFORM BLOCK-DIRECT-CASES
     PERFORM BIOME-CASES
     PERFORM PUT-ERROR-CASES
     PERFORM GET-ERROR-CASES
     PERFORM GET-WIDTH-CASES
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     STOP RUN.

*> ---- single value ----
 SINGLE-CASES.
     MOVE "block single value 1" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-KIND WS-BITS
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-BASE WS-STEP WS-MODULUS WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 2 TO WS-LENGTH WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "0001" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block single value 300 (two-byte VarInt)" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 300 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 3 TO WS-LENGTH WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "00ac02" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "biome single value 0" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 64 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 7 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-LENGTH WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "0000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM PUT-CASE.

*> ---- block states, indirect: bits byte 1 to 4 pack at 4 bits, 5 to 8 at their own width ----
 BLOCK-INDIRECT-CASES.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 1 TO WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE "block indirect 4 bits, palette 0 1, 256 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 4 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 2 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-STEP
     MOVE 2052 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 12 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "040200011010101010101010" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "1010101010101010" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block indirect bits byte 2 still packs at 4 bits (06 5.3)" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 2 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 3 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 5 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 2053 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 13 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "02030506070210210210210210" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "0210210210210210" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block indirect 5 bits, 20 ids, 342 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 5 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 20 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 100 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 2758 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 30 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "0514646566676869" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "6a6b6c6d6e6f7071727374757677" TO WS-HEX(17:28)
     MOVE "05a928398a418820" TO WS-HEX(45:16)
     MOVE "000000000007b9ac" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block indirect 6 bits, 40 two-byte ids, 410 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 6 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 40 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 200 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 3362 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 10 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "0628c801c901ca01cb01" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "00000003ce34c2ca" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block indirect 7 bits, 100 ids, 456 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 7 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 100 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 300 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 3850 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 8 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "0764ac02ad02ae02" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "000000000000005f" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block indirect 8 bits, 256 ids (VarInt 256 = 8002), 512 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 8 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 256 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 300 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 4611 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 9 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "088002ac02ad02ae02" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "fffefdfcfbfaf9f8" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE.

*> ---- block states, direct at 16 bits (4 per Long, 1024 Longs) ----
 BLOCK-DIRECT-CASES.
     MOVE "block direct 16 bits, entry i = i * 7 mod 35723, 1024 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 2 TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 16 TO WS-BITS WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-BASE WS-STEP
     MOVE 35723 TO WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 7 TO WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 8193 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 9 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "100015000e00070000" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "6ff96ff26feb6fe4" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "block direct 9 bits (first width that is Global), 7 per Long, 586 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 9 TO WS-BITS WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 512 TO WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 4689 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 9 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "090180a04018080200" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "00000000000001ff" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE.

*> ---- biomes ----
 BIOME-CASES.
     MOVE 64 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 1 TO WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 1 TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-STEP
     MOVE 7 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE "biome indirect 1 bit, palette 0 1, one Long" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 1 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 2 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 12 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 12 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "010200" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "01aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" TO WS-HEX(7:18)
     MOVE "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "biome indirect 2 bits, palette 0 to 3, two Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 2 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 4 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 22 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 22 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "020400010203e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "biome indirect 3 bits, palette 0 to 7, four Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 3 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 8 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 42 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 18 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "03080001020304050607" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "4688fac688fac688" TO WS-HEX(21:16)
     MOVE "0000000000000007" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "biome direct 7 bits (registry of 65), 9 per Long, 8 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 2 TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 7 TO WS-BITS WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT
     MOVE 65 TO WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 3 TO WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 65 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 9 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "07182a4878c1218180" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "000000000000003b" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE
     MOVE "biome direct 6 bits (registry of 64), 10 per Long, 7 Longs" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 6 TO WS-BITS WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 64 TO WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 57 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 9 TO WS-PREFIX
     MOVE "0606d85523cc2460c0" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "0000000000f7adf4" TO WS-TAIL
     PERFORM PUT-CASE.

*> ---- writer rejections: PB-ERROR set and nothing appended ----
 PUT-ERROR-CASES.
     MOVE "entry count 100 is neither 4096 nor 64" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 100 TO PB-PC-ENTRIES
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "unknown kind 3" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 3 TO PB-PC-KIND
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "single value with a palette of 2" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 0 TO PB-PC-KIND
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "single value negative" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 0 TO PB-PC-KIND
     MOVE 1 TO PB-PC-PALETTE-COUNT
     MOVE -1 TO PB-PC-PALETTE(1)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect with an empty palette" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 0 TO PB-PC-PALETTE-COUNT
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect block bits byte 0" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 0 TO PB-PC-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect block bits byte 9" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 9 TO PB-PC-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect biome bits byte 4" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 64 TO PB-PC-ENTRIES
     MOVE 4 TO PB-PC-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect 4 bits with 17 palette entries" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 17 TO PB-PC-PALETTE-COUNT
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect biome 1 bit with 3 palette entries" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 64 TO PB-PC-ENTRIES
     MOVE 1 TO PB-PC-BITS
     MOVE 3 TO PB-PC-PALETTE-COUNT
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect negative palette id" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE -5 TO PB-PC-PALETTE(2)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect entry index at the palette size" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE 2 TO PB-PC-VALUE(4096)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "indirect negative entry index" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-INDIRECT
     MOVE -1 TO PB-PC-VALUE(7)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "direct block bits 8 would read back as HashMap" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-DIRECT
     MOVE 8 TO PB-PC-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED-GLOBAL-8
     MOVE "direct bits differ from the global bits" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-DIRECT
     MOVE 15 TO PB-PC-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "direct bits above 31 (ids are BINARY-LONG)" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-DIRECT
     MOVE 32 TO PB-PC-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED-GLOBAL-32
     MOVE "direct value beyond the width" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-DIRECT
     MOVE 65536 TO PB-PC-VALUE(10)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "direct negative value" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM BASE-DIRECT
     MOVE -1 TO PB-PC-VALUE(10)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED.

*> ---- reader rejections: PB-ERROR, PB-POS back at the start, a cleared record ----
 GET-ERROR-CASES.
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE "get: entry count 100 is neither 4096 nor 64" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "0001" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     MOVE 100 TO WS-ENTRIES
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE "get: single value negative (VarInt -1)" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00ffffffff0f" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: indirect palette of 0" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "0400" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: negative palette size" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "04ffffffff0f" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: 4-bit palette of 17" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "0411" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: biome 1-bit palette of 3" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "0103000102" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     MOVE 64 TO WS-ENTRIES
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE "get: negative palette id" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "0402ffffffff0f01" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM PUT-WIRE-LONGS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: entry index beyond the palette" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 4 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 2 TO WS-LONG
     PERFORM WIRE-INDIRECT
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: short data (10 of 2048 bytes)" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "04020001" & "00000000000000000000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: Global with global bits 0" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 9 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE "09" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM FILL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: Global with global bits 32" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 32 TO WS-GLOBAL
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE "get: empty buffer" TO WS-LABEL
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED.

*> ---- the bits byte alone picks the kind; Global ignores the byte's value ----
 GET-WIDTH-CASES.
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE "block bits byte 12 reads as Global at the 16 global bits" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 12 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LONG
     PERFORM WIRE-DIRECT
     MOVE "0 0 2 12 4096 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM GET-WIDTH-CHECK
     MOVE "biome bits byte 9 reads as Global at the 7 global bits" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 64 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 7 TO WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE 9 TO WS-BITS
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 9 TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LONG
     PERFORM 8 TIMES
         CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "0 0 2 9 64 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM GET-WIDTH-CHECK.

*> ---- helpers ----

*> Builds PB-PALETTE-CONTAINER from the WS-* inputs, writes it and checks the length, the first
*> WS-PREFIX bytes (WS-HEX), the last 8 bytes (WS-TAIL, none when spaces) and the round trip.
 PUT-CASE.
     PERFORM FILL-RECORD
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-PALETTE-CONTAINER" USING PB-BUFFER PB-PALETTE-CONTAINER WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk-palette " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) ": length and error"
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-I
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-EDIT
     STRING "0 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk-palette " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) ": first bytes"
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OFFSET
     MOVE WS-PREFIX TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-HEX TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-SLICE-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OFFSET WS-COUNT TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     IF WS-TAIL NOT = SPACES
         MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
         STRING "test chunk-palette " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) ": last Long"
             DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
         COMPUTE WS-OFFSET = PB-LENGTH - 8
         MOVE 8 TO WS-COUNT
         MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
         MOVE WS-TAIL TO TL-EXPECTED
         CALL "TEST-BUFFER-SLICE-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OFFSET WS-COUNT TL-OBSERVED
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     END-IF
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     PERFORM DC-GET
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk-palette " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) ": round trip"
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SAME
     IF DC-PALETTE-CONTAINER = PB-PALETTE-CONTAINER
         MOVE 1 TO WS-SAME
     END-IF
     MOVE "1 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-SAME TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     COMPUTE WS-I = PB-LENGTH - PB-POS
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> Record: kind, bits, entries, palette base + step * (k - 1), entry i = (i - 1) * multiplier mod
*> modulus for indirect and direct containers (zero for single value).
 FILL-RECORD.
     INITIALIZE PB-PALETTE-CONTAINER
     MOVE WS-KIND TO PB-PC-KIND
     MOVE WS-BITS TO PB-PC-BITS
     MOVE WS-ENTRIES TO PB-PC-ENTRIES
     MOVE WS-PALETTE-COUNT TO PB-PC-PALETTE-COUNT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-PALETTE-COUNT
         COMPUTE PB-PC-PALETTE(WS-I) = WS-BASE + WS-STEP * (WS-I - 1)
     END-PERFORM
     IF WS-KIND NOT = 0
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-ENTRIES
             COMPUTE PB-PC-VALUE(WS-I) = FUNCTION MOD((WS-I - 1) * WS-MULTIPLIER, WS-MODULUS)
         END-PERFORM
     END-IF.

*> The reference container of the rejection cases: blocks, indirect, bits 4, palette 0 1.
 BASE-INDIRECT.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 4 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 2 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-STEP WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     PERFORM FILL-RECORD.

 BASE-DIRECT.
     MOVE 2 TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 16 TO WS-BITS
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-ENTRIES
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PALETTE-COUNT
     MOVE 200 TO WS-MODULUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-MULTIPLIER
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL
     PERFORM FILL-RECORD.

 PUT-REJECTED-GLOBAL-8.
     MOVE 8 TO WS-GLOBAL
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED.

 PUT-REJECTED-GLOBAL-32.
     MOVE 32 TO WS-GLOBAL
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED.

 PUT-REJECTED.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-PALETTE-CONTAINER" USING PB-BUFFER PB-PALETTE-CONTAINER WS-GLOBAL
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk-palette put rejects " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 16 TO WS-GLOBAL.

*> Reads the buffer into DC with WS-ENTRIES and WS-GLOBAL.
 DC-GET.
     INITIALIZE DC-PALETTE-CONTAINER
     MOVE WS-ENTRIES TO DC-PC-ENTRIES
     CALL "PB-GET-PALETTE-CONTAINER" USING PB-BUFFER DC-PALETTE-CONTAINER WS-GLOBAL.

*> The buffer must be rejected: error, position 0, and a record of kind 0 with no palette.
 GET-REJECTED.
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS PB-ERROR
     PERFORM DC-GET
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk-palette get rejects " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1 0 0 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE PB-POS TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE DC-PC-KIND TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE DC-PC-PALETTE-COUNT TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE DC-PC-VALUE(1) TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> Buffer: bits byte WS-BITS, palette 0 1, then 256 Longs of which the first is WS-LONG.
 WIRE-INDIRECT.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE WS-BITS TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LONG
     PERFORM 255 TIMES
         CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     END-PERFORM.

*> Buffer: bits byte WS-BITS then 1024 Longs of 16-bit entries, the first Long WS-LONG.
 WIRE-DIRECT.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE WS-BITS TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LONG
     PERFORM 1023 TIMES
         CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     END-PERFORM.

*> The 256 Longs of a 4-bit container after the palette already in the buffer.
 PUT-WIRE-LONGS.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LONG
     PERFORM 256 TIMES
         CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LONG
     END-PERFORM.

 FILL.
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-HEX PB-BUFFER.

 START-OBSERVED.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR.

 ADD-NUMBER-I.
     MOVE WS-I TO WS-EDIT
     IF WS-PTR > 1
         STRING " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-IF
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR.

 GET-WIDTH-CHECK.
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS PB-ERROR
     PERFORM DC-GET
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk-palette get " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     COMPUTE WS-I = PB-LENGTH - PB-POS
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE DC-PC-KIND TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE DC-PC-BITS TO WS-I
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER-I
     MOVE DC-PC-ENTRIES TO WS-I
